@startuml RestroVibes - Access Control and RBAC
!theme plain
title RestroVibes - Access Control & Role-Based Access (RBAC)

actor Client as C
actor Restaurateur as R
actor Admin as A
participant "Frontend\n(React SPA)" as FE
participant "Express API" as API
participant "Auth Middleware\n(authenticateToken)" as Auth
participant "JWT Verify\n(decodeToken)" as JWT
participant "PostgreSQL" as DB

== REGISTRATION (Role Assignment) ==

C -> FE : Sign up as Client
FE -> API : POST /api/auth/register\n{ name, email, password, role: "client" }
API -> API : Allowed roles: ["client", "restaurateurs"]
API -> DB : Create user (role = "client")
API --> FE : 201 { user, tokens }

R -> FE : Sign up as Restaurateur
FE -> API : POST /api/auth/register\n{ name, email, password, role: "restaurateurs",\nlatitude, longitude, seat_capacity, ... }
API -> API : Allowed roles: ["client", "restaurateurs"]
API -> DB : Create user (role = "restaurateurs")\n+ store GPS location + capacity
API --> FE : 201 { user, tokens }

A -> FE : Create user via Admin Panel
FE -> API : POST /api/auth/register\n(Authorization: Bearer <adminToken>)
API -> JWT : Verify token, check role = "admin"
JWT --> API : Admin confirmed
API -> API : Allowed roles: ["client", "restaurateurs", "admin"]
API -> DB : Create user with specified role
API --> FE : 201 { user info } (no auto-login)

== LOGIN (Role-Specific Sessions) ==

C -> FE : Login as Client\n{ email, password, role: "client" }
FE -> API : POST /api/auth/login\n{ email, password, role: "client" }
API -> DB : findOne({ email, role: "client" })
DB --> API : User found
API -> API : Generate JWT (role = "client")
API --> FE : { accessToken, refreshToken }

note over DB : Same email can have separate\naccounts for different roles\n(e.g., client + restaurateur)

== AUTHENTICATED REQUEST (JWT Validation) ==

FE -> API : GET /api/resource\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>
API -> Auth : Extract Bearer token
Auth -> JWT : jwt.verify(token, JWT_SECRET)
JWT --> Auth : decoded = { id, role, iat, exp }
Auth -> DB : UsersModel.findByPk(decoded.id)
DB --> Auth : User exists + active
Auth -> Auth : Attach req.user = user record
Auth -> API : Forward to route handler

== ROLE-BASED ENFORCEMENT (Controller Level) ==

== Client Permissions ==
C -> API : POST /api/appointments/\n{ service_id, date, party_size }
API -> JWT : decodeToken(token)
JWT --> API : role = "client", id = 42
API -> API : Verify: clientId matches caller
API --> C : Appointment created

C -x API : PUT /api/appointments/:id/confirm
note right of C : BLOCKED: Only restaurateur\nor admin can confirm

== Restaurateur Permissions ==
R -> API : PUT /api/appointments/:id/confirm
API -> JWT : decodeToken(token)
JWT --> API : role = "restaurateurs", id = 15
API -> DB : Fetch appointment
API -> API : Verify: appointment.restaurateurId == 15
API -> DB : Update status -> "accepted"
API --> R : Confirmed

R -x API : DELETE /api/users/delete/:id
note right of R : BLOCKED: Only admin\ncan delete users

== Admin Permissions ==
A -> API : PUT /api/appointments/:id/cancel\n(Any appointment)
API -> JWT : decodeToken(token)
JWT --> API : role = "admin"
API -> API : Admin bypass: no ownership check
API -> DB : Update status -> "cancelled"
API --> A : Cancelled

A -> API : POST /api/lottery/resolve\n{ restaurantId, bookingDate, timeSlot }
API -> Auth : Inline middleware:\nreq.user.role !== "admin" -> 403
Auth --> API : Admin confirmed
API -> API : Run weighted lottery manually
API --> A : Lottery resolved

A -> API : DELETE /api/users/delete/:id
API -> JWT : decodeToken(token)
JWT --> API : role = "admin"
API -> API : Verify: target is not also admin
API -> DB : Cancel user's appointments\n+ Delete user record
API --> A : User deleted

@enduml
